From 2f33c9ba59f240009efc227a6c123f45ba122885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:01:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(guide): the Guide answers on the brain the pill names,
 Fast by default

creative_guide.respond hardcoded resolve_brain("reasoning"), so every
Guide turn ran on Gemini 3.1 Pro with thinking HIGH -- ~1.5c a message
(26 turns, $0.37, off llm_calls), a third of a whole nightly graph run
for "which of these directions?" -- while the composer's Fast /
Reasoning pill only ever reached Create.

Now: the route reads `brain` off the form and clamps it against
gemini_utils.BRAINS exactly as scenes_run does; respond() takes it, with
creative_guide.DEFAULT_BRAIN = "fast" when nothing is sent; the fast
tier's None config becomes a bare GenerateContentConfig so the system
instruction and the response schema still attach; the job result
carries `brain` (None on a personal connection, which has no tier). The
React composer sends the pill on Guide turns as it does on Create, and
the pill's heading reads "Which model answers" in Guide mode.

Expected: ~0.4c a chat turn on Flash; flip the pill to Reasoning for
the turn that writes the brief. The personal ChatGPT/Claude path is
untouched.

Tests: the reasoning assertion now asks for it explicitly; default and
unknown tiers resolve to Fast with fallbacks allowed and no thinking
config; the route clamps reasoning/REASONING/ultra/"" -> reasoning/
reasoning/fast/fast and reports it. 2205 passed / 8 xfailed the way CI
runs it; ruff clean; next build + eslint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01H5JXJGaRzsQC4VpSGuutaH
